(3474303, 485841, 40580, '<td valign="top">Oh, I like the lighting.  I also like the energy she has, it makes me want to dance.  Good luck.</td>', 'Oh, I like the lighting.  I also like the energy she has, it makes me want to dance.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:08:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474307, 485855, 40580, '<td valign="top">I first saw the title and was expecting a nice soft light, but that''s too harsh lighting.  Make be feel cold.<br/> <br/>Great focus on the eyes.  Good luck.</td>', 'I first saw the title and was expecting a nice soft light, but that''s too harsh lighting.  Make be feel cold. Great focus on the eyes.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:09:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474308, 485695, 40580, '<td valign="top">Oh, I like.  Nothing to improve.  I like the low key nature of this shot.  Good luck.</td>', 'Oh, I like.  Nothing to improve.  I like the low key nature of this shot.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:10:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474312, 485148, 40580, '<td valign="top">If I was gay, I''d be so over him, but I don''t think my wife would alow it.  I was expecting a girl in this shot.<br/> <br/>I do like the focus on the eyes.  Good luck.</td>', 'If I was gay, I''d be so over him, but I don''t think my wife would alow it.  I was expecting a girl in this shot. I do like the focus on the eyes.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:12:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474314, 484328, 40580, '<td valign="top">It''s a little soft.  Try a faster shutter speed.  Also, the highlights in her eyes are distracting.  Get the light source up and away from the camera.<br/> <br/>Good Luck.</td>', 'It''s a little soft.  Try a faster shutter speed.  Also, the highlights in her eyes are distracting.  Get the light source up and away from the camera. Good Luck.', '2007-03-19 23:14:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474316, 485780, 40580, '<td valign="top">Is she shy?  It would be more stunning if she was looking at the camera.</td>', 'Is she shy?  It would be more stunning if she was looking at the camera.', '2007-03-19 23:14:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474321, 484256, 40580, '<td valign="top">Are you on the roof?  Nice shot.  Nothing to improve except softer lighting, but that''s hard to do when there''s not clouds.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'Are you on the roof?  Nice shot.  Nothing to improve except softer lighting, but that''s hard to do when there''s not clouds. Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:15:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474326, 485312, 40580, '<td valign="top">Oh, I like.  I would''ve thought the red thing on the left would be distracting, but you don''t notice it with the great contrasting colors (blue and red).  Maybe that''s the only thing wrong with this shot (the red thing on the left).<br/> <br/>Great shot and focus on the eyes.  Good luck.</td>', 'Oh, I like.  I would''ve thought the red thing on the left would be distracting, but you don''t notice it with the great contrasting colors (blue and red).  Maybe that''s the only thing wrong with this shot (the red thing on the left). Great shot and focus on the eyes.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:17:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474335, 484487, 40580, '<td valign="top">The colors look off in his face.  Maybe it''s because it matches with the grey background.  Almost looks dead.<br/> <br/>Watch the highlights on the medals.  Those are hard to photograph in hard lighting.  Try softening the light.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'The colors look off in his face.  Maybe it''s because it matches with the grey background.  Almost looks dead. Watch the highlights on the medals.  Those are hard to photograph in hard lighting.  Try softening the light. Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:19:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474338, 484991, 40580, '<td valign="top">The color is off.  Her complexion has too majenta.  Good luck.</td>', 'The color is off.  Her complexion has too majenta.  Good luck.', '2007-03-19 23:22:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474344, 485808, 40580, '<td valign="top">Oh, great shot.  I love the depth of view.  The bench and background add to the shot.  Great focus on the eyes.  I hope it does well.</td>', 'Oh, great shot.  I love the depth of view.  The bench and background add to the shot.  Great focus on the eyes.  I hope it does well.', '2007-03-19 23:23:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474346, 485808, 70484, '<td valign="top">He looks so sad...Nice capture though.</td>', 'He looks so sad...Nice capture though.', '2007-03-19 23:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474347, 484797, 40580, '<td valign="top">His skin tone is too blue and cold for me.  Also, that thing in the lower middle and left is too distracting.</td>', 'His skin tone is too blue and cold for me.  Also, that thing in the lower middle and left is too distracting.', '2007-03-19 23:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474348, 485286, 73601, '<td valign="top">great eyes</td>', 'great eyes', '2007-03-19 23:25:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474353, 484403, 64489, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot a lot.  The composition and balance of the subjects are very nice, and the background is appropriate with beautiful bokeh.  I also like the contrast on the model''s faces; it really adds some depth to the shot.  Somehow her eyes feel just a bit too oversaturated for my tastes... I know many voters here seem to love that extremely pure tone, but I feel it''s a little unnatural and actually on the side of feeling over processed for me.  That being said, I think my biggest gripe is actually not the photo itself but rather the border; while I feel the thin band of color is simple and appropriate to use, it feels a little warmer/saturated compared to the bulk of the rest of the picture and I would rather the subjects maintain the focal vibrance.  That in no way has anything to do with the actual photograph, however, and I''m not going to let a border affect my rating; just an impression I have of the overall presentation.  Great job.</td>', 'I really like this shot a lot.  The composition and balance of the subjects are very nice, and the background is appropriate with beautiful bokeh.  I also like the contrast on the model''s faces; it really adds some depth to the shot.  Somehow her eyes feel just a bit too oversaturated for my tastes... I know many voters here seem to love that extremely pure tone, but I feel it''s a little unnatural and actually on the side of feeling over processed for me.  That being said, I think my biggest gripe is actually not the photo itself but rather the border; while I feel the thin band of color is simple and appropriate to use, it feels a little warmer/saturated compared to the bulk of the rest of the picture and I would rather the subjects maintain the focal vibrance.  That in no way has anything to do with the actual photograph, however, and I''m not going to let a border affect my rating; just an impression I have of the overall presentation.  Great job.', '2007-03-19 23:28:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474367, 485611, 64489, '<td valign="top">This is a really interesting shot, but I think very effective as a color portrait.  The amount of processing feels just right, and nothing is oversharpened or saturated to an unnatural level.  The expression on the subject''s face is a curious one; it feels to me like it is almost leaning toward anger, and I am not sure why that would be the choice in an obviously posed, lit portrait setting.  What is the reason for the level of sternness in the subject''s glance, in other words?  With this in mind, I love the lighting and the beautiful catch lights in his eyes, and the colors all have a balanced and complimentary tone that really enhance this photograph a lot.  Great job.</td>', 'This is a really interesting shot, but I think very effective as a color portrait.  The amount of processing feels just right, and nothing is oversharpened or saturated to an unnatural level.  The expression on the subject''s face is a curious one; it feels to me like it is almost leaning toward anger, and I am not sure why that would be the choice in an obviously posed, lit portrait setting.  What is the reason for the level of sternness in the subject''s glance, in other words?  With this in mind, I love the lighting and the beautiful catch lights in his eyes, and the colors all have a balanced and complimentary tone that really enhance this photograph a lot.  Great job.', '2007-03-19 23:33:14.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3474373, 483951, 73601, '<td valign="top">very pixelated</td>', 'very pixelated', '2007-03-19 23:37:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474378, 484695, 64489, '<td valign="top">What a bold, engaging photograph!  First, I must say that I really love the color, the expression of the subject, and the texture used throughout.  It''s a really unique and powerful photo and my guess is it is going to do extremely well.  My critique would be that it feels a bit overprocessed to me - slightly to a detrimental level - and I think this shot could actually be enhanced by holding back just a little.  The eyes in particular, while certainly striking and colorful, are just a bit too sharp and in high contrast in relation to the rest of the picture.  While they certainly grab your focus, they also feel somewhat less genuine in the context of this photo for me.  Her cheeks also look a tad saturated, almost as if all of the pink color was entirely added in post (maybe it was?).  Other than that, you made a very bold compositional/angle choice, the color of the entire image is fantastic, and the subject is both enchanting and beautiful.  Great job.</td>', 'What a bold, engaging photograph!  First, I must say that I really love the color, the expression of the subject, and the texture used throughout.  It''s a really unique and powerful photo and my guess is it is going to do extremely well.  My critique would be that it feels a bit overprocessed to me - slightly to a detrimental level - and I think this shot could actually be enhanced by holding back just a little.  The eyes in particular, while certainly striking and colorful, are just a bit too sharp and in high contrast in relation to the rest of the picture.  While they certainly grab your focus, they also feel somewhat less genuine in the context of this photo for me.  Her cheeks also look a tad saturated, almost as if all of the pink color was entirely added in post (maybe it was?).  Other than that, you made a very bold compositional/angle choice, the color of the entire image is fantastic, and the subject is both enchanting and beautiful.  Great job.', '2007-03-19 23:37:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474383, 484527, 73601, '<td valign="top">very crisp</td>', 'very crisp', '2007-03-19 23:40:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474387, 484610, 64489, '<td valign="top">I really like this photograph a lot; even though the subject is simple, it''s completely appropriate and very well framed.  I would go so far as to say as I think this picture felt the most "professional" to me in the lot, in as much as I could easily see it in a magazine or the like.  The composition is very strong, the lighting is great, the focus is tack sharp, and the colors are all complimentary of each other.  I feel like there are some other photographs in the challenge which have just a tad more originality to them, but on the technical level this one is really great.  Good job.</td>', 'I really like this photograph a lot; even though the subject is simple, it''s completely appropriate and very well framed.  I would go so far as to say as I think this picture felt the most "professional" to me in the lot, in as much as I could easily see it in a magazine or the like.  The composition is very strong, the lighting is great, the focus is tack sharp, and the colors are all complimentary of each other.  I feel like there are some other photographs in the challenge which have just a tad more originality to them, but on the technical level this one is really great.  Good job.', '2007-03-19 23:41:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474395, 485036, 64489, '<td valign="top">What a lovely shot.  I really love the personality in this photo, as well as its simple nature and non-reliance on post processing to carry it through.  I definitely had to do a double take to tell if they were really twins or not (and that''s a testament to the picture, for sure)! :-)  My biggest complaint would be that I feel you could have either closed the aperture to get both boys in focus, or perhaps instead, shifted the focus to the subject who is facing us and making the connection with the viewer.  Although the boy in the foreground is closer, he is looking off to the side and isn''t, in my eyes, where I want the focus to be: right at the catchlights in the eyes of the boy who is looking right at us.  Other than that, a beautiful picture with a lot of heart and nice, appropriate colors throughout.  Great job.</td>', 'What a lovely shot.  I really love the personality in this photo, as well as its simple nature and non-reliance on post processing to carry it through.  I definitely had to do a double take to tell if they were really twins or not (and that''s a testament to the picture, for sure)! :-)  My biggest complaint would be that I feel you could have either closed the aperture to get both boys in focus, or perhaps instead, shifted the focus to the subject who is facing us and making the connection with the viewer.  Although the boy in the foreground is closer, he is looking off to the side and isn''t, in my eyes, where I want the focus to be: right at the catchlights in the eyes of the boy who is looking right at us.  Other than that, a beautiful picture with a lot of heart and nice, appropriate colors throughout.  Great job.', '2007-03-19 23:47:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474472, 485828, 70000, '<td valign="top">intense, i wish the table wasn''t so shiny because it looks like his trapped behind a nice table and a cool living room, maybe a roughed up table would work better?</td>', 'intense, i wish the table wasn''t so shiny because it looks like his trapped behind a nice table and a cool living room, maybe a roughed up table would work better?', '2007-03-20 00:46:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(3474474, 483871, 74209, '<td valign="top">Perfect title.  From this one thought all the storms of childhood. Your composition captures the fury of nature and the almost unreadable expression in the face of this lovely child.  Well done!</td>', 'Perfect title.  From this one thought all the storms of childhood. Your composition captures the fury of nature and the almost unreadable expression in the face of this lovely child.  Well done!', '2007-03-20 00:50:33.000000', NULL, 1),
