(3482821, 483282, 41337, '<td valign="top">Your photo is pretty good. The lighting on the face and the composition especially. <br/> <br/>I do have an issue with that back spotlight though. For me it''s too bright and takes the focus away from the face. To fix that in post, I would simplify things by first converting to black and white that way the color is no longer a visual element that demands it''s own attention. I''d also lower the highlights just a tad while deepening the shadows a little. I tried this in photoshop and it seems to work as my eyes are drawn to his a lot quicker. Basically what happens is the eyes are a bit darker and thus pop more pulling the focus away from the bright spot. Anyway, just a thought.</td>', 'Your photo is pretty good. The lighting on the face and the composition especially.  I do have an issue with that back spotlight though. For me it''s too bright and takes the focus away from the face. To fix that in post, I would simplify things by first converting to black and white that way the color is no longer a visual element that demands it''s own attention. I''d also lower the highlights just a tad while deepening the shadows a little. I tried this in photoshop and it seems to work as my eyes are drawn to his a lot quicker. Basically what happens is the eyes are a bit darker and thus pop more pulling the focus away from the bright spot. Anyway, just a thought.', '2007-03-23 03:30:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(3482823, 485466, 41337, '<td valign="top">Your SPs are always so well done.</td>', 'Your SPs are always so well done.', '2007-03-23 03:38:19.000000', NULL, 1),
