(3488372, 485242, 48471, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MilesW:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the idea of the perfect people in the advert contrasting with the lady in the bus, but I find my eyes being drawn to the advert and red plumage alternately, which means the central subject doesn''t get the attention it deserves. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s an extra point, no, I think that''s the whole point of this shot: how much time/attention/consideration are you (and by you I don''t mean you in particular) willing to give to the real person/human, instead to the pop/served "beauty"?</td>', 'Originally posted by MilesW: I like the idea of the perfect people in the advert contrasting with the lady in the bus, but I find my eyes being drawn to the advert and red plumage alternately, which means the central subject doesn''t get the attention it deserves.   That''s an extra point, no, I think that''s the whole point of this shot: how much time/attention/consideration are you (and by you I don''t mean you in particular) willing to give to the real person/human, instead to the pop/served "beauty"?', '2007-03-26 08:49:49.000000', NULL, 0),
