(3489265, 485518, 30982, '<td valign="top">You''ve definitely got the "Color" part of Color Portrait covered!  Not a conventional entry, that''s for sure.  Eyewave''s comment is a bit harsh, but he did point out that for some reason you have a thin white border on the left and top.  Not sure if that''s something that occurred after you loaded the shot or not.</td>', 'You''ve definitely got the "Color" part of Color Portrait covered!  Not a conventional entry, that''s for sure.  Eyewave''s comment is a bit harsh, but he did point out that for some reason you have a thin white border on the left and top.  Not sure if that''s something that occurred after you loaded the shot or not.', '2007-03-26 16:39:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3489266, 485814, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great angle and a great smile from your model!  I like the way you''ve framed her in the shot, but agree that cropping out the stripe on her pants would improve the shot - it''s a wee bit eye-catching then takes a minute to realize what it is.  Very natural and real - nice work!</td>', 'Great angle and a great smile from your model!  I like the way you''ve framed her in the shot, but agree that cropping out the stripe on her pants would improve the shot - it''s a wee bit eye-catching then takes a minute to realize what it is.  Very natural and real - nice work!', '2007-03-26 16:41:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3489271, 485587, 24389, '<td valign="top">This was one of my 10s, I love it! Congrats on the PB!</td>', 'This was one of my 10s, I love it! Congrats on the PB!', '2007-03-26 16:42:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3489272, 483128, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very good shot, Kashi - some of the comments in the thread you started will give you ideas how to change things the next time around, but the main thing is you''ve got great control on your lighting and your focus, and very good looking models to work with.  :-)  In this case, I think I''d have preferred him looking at the camera - show us those big brown eyes!</td>', 'I think this is a very good shot, Kashi - some of the comments in the thread you started will give you ideas how to change things the next time around, but the main thing is you''ve got great control on your lighting and your focus, and very good looking models to work with.  :-)  In this case, I think I''d have preferred him looking at the camera - show us those big brown eyes!', '2007-03-26 16:43:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3489273, 485855, 6388, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mattmac:</b></div><hr/><i> I thought this was yours...another beautiful portrait, but I can''t picture you coming up with the title - "Nah, P wouldn''t say ''Cozy''".<br/>:) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you haven''t seen my hidden softer, gentler side.  i like warm walks on the beach and kittens too.<br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'Originally posted by mattmac: I thought this was yours...another beautiful portrait, but I can''t picture you coming up with the title - "Nah, P wouldn''t say ''Cozy''".:)   you haven''t seen my hidden softer, gentler side.  i like warm walks on the beach and kittens too. :)', '2007-03-26 16:44:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3489279, 485704, 24389, '<td valign="top">Geez, I wish I looked good like that with a cold! btw this one was my fav and i was rooting for the blue. good luck next time.</td>', 'Geez, I wish I looked good like that with a cold! btw this one was my fav and i was rooting for the blue. good luck next time.', '2007-03-26 16:46:58.000000', NULL, 0),
