(3492730, 485426, 20608, '<td valign="top">So sorry my friend... but it takes nothing away from the fact that this is a beautiful image and one you can be very proud of.. Adding to my FAVS</td>', 'So sorry my friend... but it takes nothing away from the fact that this is a beautiful image and one you can be very proud of.. Adding to my FAVS', '2007-03-28 01:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3492825, 485810, 53814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lerin:</b></div><hr/><i> i think this deserved way better. its unique,  i dont know what it is but i dont think im supposed to. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I always thought a 3d sonogram of a baby''s face would make a great portrait. This is as close as I could come with what I had to work with - an orange lollipop with gum inside. By the time I ate enough of the lollipop to realize that there was no cute, scrunched-up face inside, I was physically ill (it was leftover halloween candy), but still was able to compose myself enough to process and enter the challenge. Part of the photo slightly resembles an embryo with a head and little arms. The rest of the photo could be a futuristic cloning lab. Yes? <br/>Welcome to DPC, Lerin.</td>', 'Originally posted by Lerin: i think this deserved way better. its unique,  i dont know what it is but i dont think im supposed to.   I always thought a 3d sonogram of a baby''s face would make a great portrait. This is as close as I could come with what I had to work with - an orange lollipop with gum inside. By the time I ate enough of the lollipop to realize that there was no cute, scrunched-up face inside, I was physically ill (it was leftover halloween candy), but still was able to compose myself enough to process and enter the challenge. Part of the photo slightly resembles an embryo with a head and little arms. The rest of the photo could be a futuristic cloning lab. Yes? Welcome to DPC, Lerin.', '2007-03-28 02:31:13.000000', NULL, 0),
