(3495504, 483586, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hello Grandad,<br/>             There are a few things I would like to point out here. First, the face board on the roof, it gives the (optical) impression that it is coming out of your should &amp; again at head level. By moving a step or two to your right would reslove this. Secondly, the pad lock again gives the (optical) impression that it it hanging from your arm, not the door. The watch on your arm there is giving off some glare that is a we bit distracting. Finally the lighting, you could have used a reflector or bounced some flash off the barn at an angle fro below to lighten up the shadow on you face. Over all I like the shot. Hope these little tid bits hlp you out.<br/> <br/>Frankie/Las Vegas</td>', 'Hello Grandad,             There are a few things I would like to point out here. First, the face board on the roof, it gives the (optical) impression that it is coming out of your should & again at head level. By moving a step or two to your right would reslove this. Secondly, the pad lock again gives the (optical) impression that it it hanging from your arm, not the door. The watch on your arm there is giving off some glare that is a we bit distracting. Finally the lighting, you could have used a reflector or bounced some flash off the barn at an angle fro below to lighten up the shadow on you face. Over all I like the shot. Hope these little tid bits hlp you out. Frankie/Las Vegas', '2007-03-28 21:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3496072, 485534, 64994, '<td valign="top">I have a shot where I used the diffuse glow filter on the model...bad idea for this site, lol. the girl LOVED the shot and I ended up at like 647 out of 705, lol. Glow bad on here, lol, at least my use of it...I like this shot a lot!! but I like the soft focus feel...so...8 in my rating system. Personally I love the look of the eyes!!! Very dreamy...<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'I have a shot where I used the diffuse glow filter on the model...bad idea for this site, lol. the girl LOVED the shot and I ended up at like 647 out of 705, lol. Glow bad on here, lol, at least my use of it...I like this shot a lot!! but I like the soft focus feel...so...8 in my rating system. Personally I love the look of the eyes!!! Very dreamy... Jack', '2007-03-29 03:25:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3496297, 485561, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> Definitely underrated. Seems like a few of the commenters didn''t like her expression. I wonder if you edited this differently if those people would have changed their mind. For example, an edit that enhanced a more somber tone say a b/w conversion with the midtones darkened. While the colors are good I wonder if that produced mix messages with what people were seeing in her expression. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the good after comment on my image, Richard.<br/>I would also have preferred to process it in b/w but with it being a Colour Portrait Challenge I had to leave it the way it was. I like the image but, as you say, her expression seemed to irritate some voters. I liked the fact that the commenters said what irritated them. At least that way, I learned something out of it.</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Definitely underrated. Seems like a few of the commenters didn''t like her expression. I wonder if you edited this differently if those people would have changed their mind. For example, an edit that enhanced a more somber tone say a b/w conversion with the midtones darkened. While the colors are good I wonder if that produced mix messages with what people were seeing in her expression.   Thanks for the good after comment on my image, Richard.I would also have preferred to process it in b/w but with it being a Colour Portrait Challenge I had to leave it the way it was. I like the image but, as you say, her expression seemed to irritate some voters. I liked the fact that the commenters said what irritated them. At least that way, I learned something out of it.', '2007-03-29 08:21:10.000000', NULL, 0),
