(4123038, 485687, 65858, '<td valign="top">You left a nice comment for me just recently in Still Life with Motion.  =)<br/> <br/>Cute shot.  A lot of folks commented on the pink.  If you have PhotoShop, use a color balance adjustment layer and play around with all nine settings (R, G, B for each of shadows, midtones, and highlights).  Just wiggle the sliders back and forth until you''re happy with it.  This is a great way to remove color casts, assuming your monitor is on target.  =)<br/> <br/>Here''s an example (and a touch of sharpening in her eyes):<br/><a href="//onetacoshort.com/upimg/preview.php?id=f4b0f9a20c9e9d8c385047a683720312" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//onetacoshort.com/upimg/f4b0f9a20c9e9d8c385047a683720312_120.jpg'', strrpos(''//onetacoshort.com/upimg/f4b0f9a20c9e9d8c385047a683720312_120.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//onetacoshort.com/upimg/f4b0f9a20c9e9d8c385047a683720312_120.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/>-Jeff<br/></td>', 'You left a nice comment for me just recently in Still Life with Motion.  =) Cute shot.  A lot of folks commented on the pink.  If you have PhotoShop, use a color balance adjustment layer and play around with all nine settings (R, G, B for each of shadows, midtones, and highlights).  Just wiggle the sliders back and forth until you''re happy with it.  This is a great way to remove color casts, assuming your monitor is on target.  =) Here''s an example (and a touch of sharpening in her eyes):  Cheers,-Jeff', '2007-09-28 18:56:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4126079, 485426, 73433, '<td valign="top">you did an amazing editing job here! i enjoy every change you made to this photo: from blurring out the objects behind the window to making the area behind her black, you did astoundingly well! bravo!</td>', 'you did an amazing editing job here! i enjoy every change you made to this photo: from blurring out the objects behind the window to making the area behind her black, you did astoundingly well! bravo!', '2007-09-30 15:46:53.000000', NULL, 0),
